## Data checks

The optional baseline needs only Python's standard library and the existing pytest dependency.
Fill in `data-checks.json` with source globs, database paths, identifier SQL types (a type string
or an object with `type` and optional namespace metadata), keys, the canonical normalizer,
connector modules, report folders and row-wise budget. Empty lists check no data; configure
real inputs before treating a passing suite as validation.

`uv run python scripts/data_checks.py data-checks.json` prints a findings table without writing
reports. `tests/test_data_checks.py` runs the same eight checks under pytest: identifier types,
keys and crosswalk uniqueness, one normalizer, connectors, stable identifiers, report lineage,
reusable processing and row-wise operations. Errors fail; warnings pass. Use `uv run pytest -s`
to see warning tables on passing tests. Removing settings skips the test with an enable message.

The pack never imports or executes project modules. Extra normalizer definitions produce an
error because sample equivalence cannot be established safely. Samples and import roots remain
metadata; the static check does not claim behavioural equivalence. A canonical module with
initialisation calls also reports an error instead of executing those calls.

SQLite opens with `immutable=1`. A nonempty WAL produces an explicit error, not a stale clean
verdict; supply a checkpointed copy made outside the inspected project. JSON reports need a
`provenance` object; text reports need a structured HTML comment carrying that object and its
required fields. Prose mentioning provenance is not a provenance block. The scan never applies
finding suppressions. Source and report scope belong in settings; warnings are advisory.
